Build, verify, install and restart all Droidloom components

Usage: droidloom-update [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  native-role-ingress-build    Build the complete framework Java library and Android JNI runtime only. Uses its independent exact source lock; does not install or enable roles
  native-generation-art-build  Build only the paired ART libraries through the normal strict source projection. Builds no image and does not install, activate, or enable a running component
  native-generation-build      Build the complete ordinary-app engine and ART APEX with strict dependencies. Uses fixed paired sources and a fresh output; does not install or grant runtime readiness
  native-generation-pair       Record the exact enabled ART/engine pair from existing product files. Does not enable a feature, build, install, or activate any component
  native-bridge-build          Rebuild the ARM64 translator in an already prepared Android workspace
  target-closure-build         Build only NativeBridge targets, deferring missing modules to Ninja errors
  native-engine-build          Build only the Android ARM64 translation engine; does not install it
  audio-apex-build             Build only the AIDL audio APEX, deferring missing modules to Ninja errors. Does not install artifacts or start services
  minigbm-build                Build the native AMD allocator candidate without installing anything
  package-stage                Compile and stage a portable pacman payload; does not install or start services
  plan                         Show the complete build plan without changing anything
  verify                       Verify an already built bundle
  help                         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>  Droidloom checkout (remembered automatically after installation)
      --clean            Delete this updater's build outputs before compiling
      --build-only       Build and verify a complete bundle without installing it
  -j, --jobs <JOBS>      Maximum parallel jobs, capped at available CPUs minus two
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version
